% FABERGÉ bibliography — real, checkable sources for the models this package
% implements. Every entry corresponds to a method actually used in src/, and
% every entry is cited from a numbered manuscript section.
%
% Two entries carried by the phase-2 scaffold were removed in the phase-5
% review because their bibliographic details could not be confirmed against a
% primary source: a "Nasdala 2004 Fabergé" note in Gems & Gemology, and a
% "Lawson 2004, hyperspectral unmixing for pigment identification" article in
% Studies in Conservation — the latter appearing to conflate Lawson & Hanson's
% 1974 NNLS monograph with the unmixing literature. An unverifiable citation is
% worse than a missing one, so they were deleted rather than reshaped.

